## Summary Takeaway

1. **`terraform state rm` (CLI method):** Immediately drops the resource from `terraform.tfstate`. It requires you to manually remove or comment out the resource block in code afterward so Terraform doesn't try to recreate it during the next plan.
2. **`removed {}` block (Code method):** A safer, code-driven approach. It allows your entire team to review state removals in code before running an apply. You must remove or comment out the matching `resource` block, or Terraform will throw a validation error.
